@comment{
  Paste your publications below in BibTeX format.
  Fastest way: Google Scholar profile -> tick the checkbox above your paper list (select all)
  -> Export -> BibTeX, then paste the result here.

  Useful extra fields (optional) for each entry:
    selected    = {true}       shows the paper in "selected publications" on the home page
    abbr        = {JCP}        small journal badge next to the entry
    doi         = {10.xxxx/...}
    pdf         = {paper.pdf}  file placed in assets/pdf/
    bibtex_show = {true}       adds a "Bib" button

  Example:
  article{mok2026example,
    title       = {Title of the paper},
    author      = {Mok, Jang and Hammes-Schiffer, Sharon},
    journal     = {The Journal of Chemical Physics},
    volume      = {164},
    pages       = {000000},
    year        = {2026},
    doi         = {10.1063/xxxxxxx},
    abbr        = {JCP},
    selected    = {true},
    bibtex_show = {true}
  }
  (Put an at-sign directly before "article" to turn this into a real entry.)
}
